===Etymology===
1859, from {{m|en|swizzle||alcoholic drink|pos=n}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|swizzle}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[utensil]], often [[disposable]], used to [[mix]] or [[stir]] [[drink]]s, commonly iced tea or [[cocktail]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The rum-based mixed drink came with a '''swizzle stick''' shaped like a pirate's sword.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1897|title=Cakes & Ale|author=Edward Spencer|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/43278/pg43278-images.html|passage=Churn up the mixture with a '''swizzle-stick''', which can be easily made with the assistance of a short length of cane (the ordinary school-treat brand) a piece of cork, a bit of string, and a pocket knife.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=[[w:Tsitsi Dangarembga|Tsitsi Dangarembga]]|title=[[w:The Book of Not|The Book of Not]]|publisher=Faber & Faber Limited (2021)|page=289|passage=Ting, ting, ting! Tracey hit her '''swizzle stick''' against her glass.}}

